1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,409
Namaste!

2
00:00:02,359 --> 00:00:10,710
In this short video, we will see how a support ticket at Fortuna now reaches the right engineer, automatically.

3
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:17,398
First the one-time setup, then we test each screen, and then the whole flow together.

4
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:20,005
Chaliye, let's begin.

5
00:00:21,412 --> 00:00:24,231
First, the big picture.

6
00:00:24,181 --> 00:00:27,000
The agent picks the customer.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,075
The serial number list shows only that customer's units, and the item name fills itself.

8
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:45,963
When the ticket is saved, the system reads the customer's Bill To address, finds the branch, picks that branch's team, and gives the ticket to an engineer who works there.

9
00:00:45,963 --> 00:00:48,729
No manual routing at all.

10
00:00:50,144 --> 00:00:52,843
Part one, the setup.

11
00:00:52,793 --> 00:00:57,022
Step one: Job Locations, on Desk.

12
00:00:57,022 --> 00:00:59,908
Each branch has one record.

13
00:00:59,908 --> 00:01:02,168
Here is Mumbai.

14
00:01:02,168 --> 00:01:09,655
Under Cities, we have Mumbai, Navi Mumbai and Thane, and under States, Maharashtra.

15
00:01:09,655 --> 00:01:16,357
One city or state belongs to only one branch, so there is never any confusion.

16
00:01:16,357 --> 00:01:21,996
And Kolkata is the default, for any address that does not match.

17
00:01:23,412 --> 00:01:26,617
Step two: the engineers.

18
00:01:26,567 --> 00:01:33,442
Open each H D Agent, and set the Job Location where that person actually sits.

19
00:01:33,442 --> 00:01:36,261
Rohit here is in Mumbai.

20
00:01:36,261 --> 00:01:39,359
Keep Availability as Active.

21
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:46,075
If someone is on leave, simply mark them Unavailable, and new tickets will skip them.

22
00:01:47,488 --> 00:01:53,047
Step three: Team Routing, inside Fortuna Support Settings.

23
00:01:52,997 --> 00:01:59,140
Each row says, this ticket type, from this branch, goes to this team.

24
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:05,257
For example, Hardware from Mumbai goes to Hardware Support, Mumbai.

25
00:02:05,257 --> 00:02:08,887
The rows without a branch are the fallback.

26
00:02:10,292 --> 00:02:14,162
Step four: check the customer's address.

27
00:02:14,112 --> 00:02:19,258
The Billing address, that is the Bill To, decides the branch.

28
00:02:19,258 --> 00:02:25,069
For Demo Client, the city is Kolkata and the state is West Bengal.

29
00:02:25,069 --> 00:02:28,221
That's it, the setup is done.

30
00:02:28,221 --> 00:02:32,582
Most of it is already created for you during the update.

31
00:02:33,984 --> 00:02:37,614
Part two, let's test each screen.

32
00:02:37,564 --> 00:02:40,423
Open Helpdesk, Tickets.

33
00:02:40,423 --> 00:02:45,663
See, the Customer column now comes right after the ticket number.

34
00:02:45,663 --> 00:02:49,559
So you know who is calling, at one glance.

35
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,921
Click Create.

36
00:02:52,871 --> 00:02:56,023
The very first field is Customer.

37
00:02:56,023 --> 00:03:00,332
And notice, there is no Job Location field here.

38
00:03:00,332 --> 00:03:03,031
Nobody has to choose it.

39
00:03:04,448 --> 00:03:08,424
Pick the customer, then open Serial Number.

40
00:03:08,374 --> 00:03:12,616
Only this customer's own five units are listed.

41
00:03:12,616 --> 00:03:17,018
Someone else's device cannot be picked by mistake.

42
00:03:18,420 --> 00:03:24,045
Choose a serial, and Item Name fills itself: Demo Model 1.

43
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:28,064
It is locked, so it always matches the unit.

44
00:03:29,464 --> 00:03:36,366
Now choose the ticket type and the subject, write a short description, and click Submit.

45
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:40,145
Bas, that's all the agent has to type.

46
00:03:41,564 --> 00:03:43,865
The ticket is saved.

47
00:03:43,815 --> 00:03:52,910
On the right, the team is Hardware Support, Kolkata, and it is already assigned to Arpan, an engineer from Kolkata.

48
00:03:54,312 --> 00:03:59,485
Open the same ticket in Desk, on the Product and Warranty tab.

49
00:03:59,435 --> 00:04:05,871
Serial number, item name, warranty, and Job Location, Kolkata.

50
00:04:05,871 --> 00:04:11,350
All filled automatically, from the unit and from the customer's address.

51
00:04:12,772 --> 00:04:16,655
One more check, from the customer's side.

52
00:04:16,605 --> 00:04:23,028
On the customer portal, the customer sees only their own units, with the item name.

53
00:04:23,028 --> 00:04:27,509
There is no Customer field, and no Job Location.

54
00:04:27,509 --> 00:04:29,810
That stays internal.

55
00:04:31,232 --> 00:04:35,820
Part three, the whole flow, with different customers.

56
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:41,062
A Mumbai customer goes to the Mumbai team and the Mumbai engineer.

57
00:04:41,062 --> 00:04:48,363
Pune is not listed as a city, but its state, Maharashtra, is, so again Mumbai.

58
00:04:48,363 --> 00:04:54,653
Chennai, or no address at all, goes to Kolkata, our head office.

59
00:04:54,653 --> 00:05:02,073
And if the agent changes the Job Location later, the team and the engineer change along with it.

60
00:05:03,492 --> 00:05:08,439
So, just pick the customer, and the system does the rest.

61
00:05:08,389 --> 00:05:13,814
Right units, right item, right branch, right engineer.

62
00:05:13,814 --> 00:05:19,413
The full guide, with every setup and test step, is in the document.

63
00:05:19,413 --> 00:05:23,043
Thank you, and all the best for your demo!

